From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] Give the modal diagnostic console its keys before keybindings

The console is a safe area: while it is open, no keybinding, Lua shortcut or input policy handler
may run on the keys typed into it. The diagnostic input bridge only saw key events after Mutter's
keybinding dispatch, so shortcuts still fired. Offer key events to the bridge first, from the
stage input-policy filter that runs before every other consumer. The bridge declines unless the
console is open, and keeps the Ctrl+Alt+F1..F12 console switches working.

diff --git a/src/core/events.c b/src/core/events.c
--- a/src/core/events.c
+++ b/src/core/events.c
@@ -409,6 +409,10 @@
   MetaDisplay *display = user_data;
 
   (void) stage;
+  /* The diagnostic console is modal: while it is open it takes key events before Lua input
+   * handlers, keybindings and shortcuts can act on them. */
+  if (gnoblin_plugin_input_handle_key (G_OBJECT (display), event))
+    return TRUE;
   return gnoblin_native_control_filter_input_event (display, event, NULL);
 }
 
